module uim.fiori_blocks.domain.valueobjects;

/// Value objects for the domain layer of the application.
/// These value objects encapsulate domain-specific concepts and ensure the integrity and consistency of the data within the domain layer.
/// Examples of value objects include Money, DateRange, and EmailAddress, among others.
/// They are immutable and are compared based on their values rather than their identities.
/// They play a crucial role in maintaining the integrity of the domain model by preventing invalid states and ensuring that business rules are consistently enforced.
/// They are an essential part of the domain-driven design approach, helping to model complex business rules and concepts accurately.
/// By using value objects, developers can create a more expressive and robust domain model that closely aligns with the business requirements.
/// This approach reduces the likelihood of errors and enhances the maintainability and readability of the code.
/// Overall, value objects contribute to a more robust and reliable domain model, promoting best practices in domain-driven design.
/// They help to encapsulate complex business logic within the domain layer, reducing the risk of inconsistencies and errors in the application.
/// By modeling these concepts as value objects, developers can create a more expressive and maintainable codebase that accurately reflects the business domain.
/// This practice ultimately leads to a higher quality software design, with clearer boundaries and more predictable behavior within the domain layer.
/// In summary, value objects are a fundamental building block in domain-driven design, providing a means to model complex business concepts accurately and consistently.
/// They help to ensure that the domain model remains expressive, maintainable, and aligned with the business requirements, ultimately leading to higher quality software.
/// By leveraging value objects effectively, developers can create a domain model that is both resilient and adaptable to changing business needs.
/// This adaptability ensures that the software can evolve alongside the business, accommodating new requirements and changes without compromising the integrity of the domain model.
/// In essence, value objects provide a foundation for building a flexible, maintainable, and high-quality domain model that can effectively support the evolving needs of the business.    4
